  "findings": [
    "Named consume and chase helper changes removed avoidable hot outlined wrappers. All inspected raw explicit scans are call-free; no surviving packet fold helper is needed. Raw and Series C1/C8 inspected hot bodies are call-free. Tuple64 retains genuine start/state prepared routes: two C1 call sites and sixteen C8 call sites.",
    "Staged field requests explicitly form SIMD ranks/addresses, then scalar byte/u16 loads construct SIMD carriers on x86; staged address/value arrays disappear in selected single-field bodies. Separate x86 gather controls emit actual VPGATHERDD plus rounded dword address, variable shift and narrow-field mask. No hardware gather is attributed to staged lanes.",
    "NEON selected explicit scan bodies use only callee-save stack locations, with no staged address/value or decoded arrays. All selected x86 F1 used and F3 checkpoint bodies are stack-free. Explicit SIMD request arithmetic uses YMM u32 in v3 and ZMM u32 in v4.",
    "Selected plane/split used bodies normalize identically per x86 mode/max/ISA, and grouped CP16/CP32 used bodies normalize identically. This isolates their shared used-field instruction route; it does not establish constant-pool identity, cache behavior or equal timing.",
    "Compound x86 AVX2 controls still have real homes: sampled F4 live-used gather has 168 B deepest own frame (40 B reservation plus 128 B red-zone). Sampled F4/F5 staged lanes save 32 B. F5 gather is stack-free on Zen and has 40 B own reservation on Granite; sampled AVX512 compound counterparts are stack-free.",
    "Native starts16 prefix widens u8/u16 lanes to u32 before accumulation. NEON uses four-lane carry, AVX2 includes eight-lane sublane carry and second-half propagation, and AVX512 propagates across sixteen lanes. Whole-group projection uses the authored native prefix/group decoders, with no generic per-row prefix helper boundary.",
    "Bulk projection has only libc memcpy hot call sites; static call-site multiplicity reflects unrolled alternatives. Source body+selected-block offset is hoisted outside individual row-copy sites for raw, Series and Tuple group consumers. Ordered copies retain compiler scalar staging; shuffled Series/TP copies retain large intentional scratch starts/lengths.",
    "Series reconstruction and Tuple prepared routing remain format-specific emitted work. This review does not replace that work with a fabricated equivalent raw decoder."
  ],
